SUMMARY:Family Hike at Sugarloaf
DESCRIPTION:Come to the park for a peaceful hike through the woods on Monday\, May 25! Join our Docents on this fun family hike that is good for all ages\, where you will learn about Sugarloaf Park\, its plants\, animals\, and history. \nThe hike begins from the Visitor Center. One option heads down to the waterfall on the Pony Gate-Canyon loop\, while a second option will meander along the Creekside Nature Trail. Please note the route is bound to change depending on logistics such as wet crossings and the participants’ physical ability. Free event\, RSVP required. Wear layers\, appropriate footwear for slippery/muddy trails\, bring at least a quart (32oz) of water\, sun protection\, and if desired\, a snack. Heavy rains cancel. Parking fees apply.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/family-hike-at-sugarloaf-4/
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
